                                        "entry_id": "812966c2-74ad-3f52-beab-601cd071d615",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An instruction in a computer program, especially one that returns no value, as opposed to a function call."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b0ed5cb-8be1-40cf-90c8-b44c1e24b704",
                                                "sense_id": "066c45ff-ee18-3f88-95cb-37bb1264a235",
                                                "text": "In this section we will examine BASIC's primary statement for repeating a string of statements under program control: the FOR statement. Another statement, the NEXT statement, is always used with a FOR statement."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49f0f390-7e73-4db4-8655-586c7909368f",
                                                "sense_id": "066c45ff-ee18-3f88-95cb-37bb1264a235",
                                                "text": "However, it is the responsibility of the programmer to ensure that the control ultimately reaches the last statement of the range."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
